NymClientTest
├── setup
│   ├── given no client exists yet
│   │   ├── it creates one
│   │   ├── it forces tls
│   │   ├── it sets a real per-request timeout
│   │   ├── it pins the client id
│   │   ├── it disables the poisson stream
│   │   └── it records that the tunnel came up
│   ├── given a client already exists
│   │   └── it reuses it
│   ├── given setup is already in flight
│   │   └── it joins the in-flight attempt
│   └── given setup itself fails
│       ├── it reports the failure
│       ├── it lets the next call try again
│       └── it records why
├── fetching
│   ├── given the request succeeds
│   │   ├── it returns the parsed body
│   │   └── it reports the status
│   ├── given the origin answers with an http error
│   │   ├── it reports transport success
│   │   ├── it does not treat the tunnel as broken
│   │   ├── it does not pass the error page off as data
│   │   └── it carries the status as the error
│   ├── given the transport throws a recoverable error
│   │   ├── it reports failure without asking for a teardown
│   │   └── it describes a thrown non-error too
│   ├── given the transport throws a fatal error
│   │   ├── given the go runtime has exited
│   │   │   └── it asks for a teardown
│   │   ├── given the gateway connection failed
│   │   │   └── it asks for a teardown
│   │   └── given the network has no more gateways
│   │       └── it asks for a teardown
│   ├── given the request ignores its cors mode
│   │   └── it passes the unsafe-ignore-cors escape hatch
│   └── given a browser user agent is required
│       ├── it sends one
│       └── it sends a complete one
├── deadlines
│   ├── given the deadline expires during setup
│   │   └── it fails rather than hanging
│   ├── given the deadline expires during the request
│   │   └── it fails rather than hanging
│   ├── given the deadline expires while reading the response
│   │   └── it fails rather than hanging
│   ├── given a timeout is not a usable number
│   │   └── it falls back to the default
│   ├── given the deadline has already passed before a step begins
│   │   └── it fails without starting the work
│   ├── withDeadline
│   │   ├── given the deadline is already in the past
│   │   │   └── it rejects without waiting
│   │   ├── given the deadline is exactly now
│   │   │   └── it rejects rather than starting the work
│   │   ├── given the promise settles first
│   │   │   ├── it resolves with the value
│   │   │   ├── it leaves no timer behind
│   │   │   ├── it leaves no timer behind when it rejects
│   │   │   └── it propagates a rejection unchanged
│   │   └── given the deadline passes first
│   │       ├── it rejects with the labelled step
│   │       └── it identifies itself as a deadline failure
│   └── given any failure at all
│       └── it returns a result rather than throwing
└── teardown
    ├── given a client exists
    │   ├── it disconnects
    │   ├── it records the teardown
    │   └── it leaves the stored identity alone
    ├── given disconnecting throws
    │   └── it still clears local state
    └── given reset is requested
        └── it drops the instance without disconnecting
